<title>ITALY: Italy raises maximum limit on net 1996 bond issues.</title>
<headline>Italy raises maximum limit on net 1996 bond issues.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian government on Thursday said it raised the maximum limit on the net issue of bonds in Italy and abroad in 1996 to 130 trillion lire from 123 trillion lire.</p>
<p>The government made the change in a decree law proposed by the Treasury Ministry and approved at a cabinet meeting.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
